windowOwnerT -- popups stroke 4 (SEQ 770, 2026-11-24; Tony's rulings 3, 5 and 7 on docs/popupsRecon.md): the popup belongs to
its form. Tester's shape, a delta of windowOkT. No window is shown. owHost has three fields: owA opens owPop (a plain popup),
owB opens owModal (a popup form carrying modal=1), owC counts its clicks (owHits). The window's own lines are read: "popup
window: X belongs to Y, no resize" (the resize word is the window's style mask read back), "window closing: Y takes its
popup X with it", and "windowClick Y: under its modal popup X, nothing fired".
Read too: owA's text in the definition, owHits, how many popups are open (targets), and which of the three forms a window
still holds (readWindow refuses by name when none does).
W-0  only owHost is open.
W-1  owA opens owPop: it belongs to owHost and has no resize. NOT MODAL: owC under it still fires (hits 1).
W-2  red is picked in the popup, then owHost is closed: owPop closes with it, as Cancel -- owA still reads first; no window
     holds either form; no target.
W-3  owHost shown again; owB opens owModal: it belongs to owHost and is modal. owC clicked: nothing fires and it says so
     (hits stays 1). owA clicked: likewise, so no second popup opens.
W-4  the modal's own Cancel, clicked in the modal's window (not blocked): it closes; owC fires again (hits 2).
W-5  owModal open again, owHost closed: the modal closes with it.
